# Keep every text file stored as LF and checked out as LF, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which rewrites line endings on
# checkout. Without this file a Windows clone and a macOS/Linux clone would disagree about every
# line ending, and the checked-out working tree would look modified straight after cloning.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary

# The PowerShell scripts carry Chinese text and are read as UTF-8 with a BOM by both Windows
# PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7, so pinning LF keeps them byte-identical everywhere.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
